 "notes": [
  "Garden landmark footprint is x11-15, y7-10 (cell collision; offset 0). Its three lamps block (10,6), (15,6) and (15,9) as in the kit; the first-lap bands are x8-9 / x17-18 / y4-5 / y12-13 plus the west walkway at x3, so every lap cell has a free 2x2 block.",
  "Counter-clockwise lap from the arrival mat: down the west walkway (x3), right along row 12, up column 17, left along row 5. The Pace floor arrows around the garden mark this 'approved route'.",
  "North wall, west to east: elevator module x2-4 (wall rows 0-1, LIFT mat row y2), call panel x5, pinboard x6-8, window x9-10, printer alcove x11-15, twin clock x16-17, meeting-room door module x18-20 (MEET mat row y2), projected form x21-24, Pace sign x25-26.",
  "Module collision is the kit's: closed and half block `111/111/000`, open leaves only the centre cell of the middle row walkable (`111/101/000`), so an open elevator or meeting-room door is a one-cell recess, not a through passage.",
  "wall_w_plain runs on rows 2-16 now that the elevator no longer interrupts the west wall (it is still an art_gap flag only until feat/art-orientation-completion merges); wall_e_plain is omitted on the Records door rows (5-7) so the door's own collision governs.",
  "The garden cut-through is the garden landmark's after state (column x12, y7-10); there is no separate north-rim placement."
 ]
